    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Josh Naylor** (64.77) and **James Wood** (64.75), our premier offensive threats against the Ryne Nelson and Michael King matchups, respectively. **Naylor** benefits significantly from hitting in the #3 hole and a favorable matchup against Nelson, while **Wood** remains an essential start despite the threat of King; his #1 spot in the lineup and elite xwOBA metrics make him a high-floor producer even in a tough park environment. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (69.83) earns the highest efficiency score of the day, with the optimizer rewarding his dynamic platoon advantage against Kumar Rocker. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** (60.40) provides the essential SB-focused production we prioritize; despite a daunting matchup against Bryan Woo, his position in the #2 hole and positive platoon splits keep his efficiency firmly in the \"Strong\" start category.\n\nBeyond the high-scorers, we are banking on a park-factor boost for **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Henry Bolte**, who both benefit from favorable conditions against Ryan Weathers, pushing their scores to 56.22 and 53.85 respectively. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Kyle Karros** (54.55), who narrowly missed the cut for our UTIL spot. While **Karros** presents a compelling case due to his strong park and SP skill ratings, the optimizer favored the structural stability and RBI potential of **Naylor**. We remain cautious regarding **Gabriel Moreno** and **Jose Caballero**, as both are battling sub-50 efficiency scores driven by stiff SP skill headwinds from Bryan Woo and J.T. Ginn. Owners should monitor official lineups closely, as our projections for **Moreno**, **Pasquantino**, **Turang**, **Caballero**, **Young**, **Riley**, **Suzuki**, **Wood**, **Soderstrom**, **Carroll**, **Bolte**, and **Naylor** are currently based on assumed batting orders; any shifts into the bottom of the order will trigger an immediate downward revision to our daily efficiency expectations.",
